The tram stops and I get off.
I am in the city centre now.
It is Saturday and the streets are very full.
There are people everywhere.
I see a bakery.
A woman is standing in front of the bakery.
I ask the woman for directions.
"Excuse me, please," I say.
"How do I get to the museums?"
The woman is very friendly.
She points to the big street.
"Go straight ahead here," she says.
"Just keep going."
"And at the end, go to the right."
"Thank you very much for your help," I say.
"You are welcome," the woman answers.
I set off.
I walk straight ahead and see many beautiful buildings.
